Real-time temperature monitor for sensors on /dev/i2cN

Syntax:
    thermd [-d /dev/i2cN] [-s ADDR]... [-T period_ms] [-D deadline_ms]
           [-H threshold_C] [-f ADDR:REG | -f none] [-P priority]
           [-t seconds] [-q]

Options:
    -d dev       I2C device (default /dev/i2c0)
    -s ADDR      LM75/TMP105-style sensor to read; repeat for more
                 (default 0x48 and 0x49, up to 4)
    -T ms        sampling period (default 10)
    -D ms        deadline for each period's work (default: the period)
    -H C         over-temperature threshold (default 80); back to normal
                 5 C below it
    -f ADDR:REG  register that turns the fan on (1) and off (0)
                 (default 0x57:0x00, a byte in an EEPROM on the bench);
                 "none" to only log
    -P prio      SCHED_FIFO priority (default 30)
    -t s         stop after this many seconds and print the report
                 (default: run until SIGINT or SIGTERM)
    -q           no once-a-second status line

The report gives minimum, median, 99th percentile and maximum of the
wake-up lateness and the response time of every period, and counts
missed deadlines. A RESULT line repeats the numbers for scripts.

If the driver dies, thermd reopens the device and logs how long it had
no data.
